BUNDLED THIRD-PARTY CODE

SQLite (via the `libsqlite3-sys` crate's `bundled-sqlcipher` feature,
which vendors and compiles the SQLite amalgamation source directly
into the binary): SQLite is public domain. See
https://www.sqlite.org/copyright.html. No separate attribution is
required by SQLite's own terms; noted here for completeness.

SQLCipher (the same `bundled-sqlcipher` feature vendors SQLCipher's
own C source alongside SQLite's, providing the transparent page-level
encryption `fossh-store`'s database uses — see DECISIONS.md for the
per-install key model): BSD-3-Clause-style license. See
https://www.zetetic.net/sqlcipher/license/. Links against the host
system's OpenSSL (`openssl-devel` at build time) rather than vendoring
its own, so no separate OpenSSL attribution is added here beyond what
a standard system OpenSSL install already carries.

